Z||000007||Carrolles||09-18-2001||07:40 AM||||I bought both battery tray parts from the dealer for around $25 US for my 85GT.  I cut the remnants of the old tray out leaving a but of a flange on the front firewall.  I pop riveted the new tray to this part and to the fender well.  Works like new.||||reg||1
Z||000008||falconhulk||09-18-2001||08:11 AM||||Thanks Carrolles!  I am very leary about moving the battery to the front.  Its not like in a muscle car where you can easily route a low guage wire through the passanger compartment.  Other then weight distrubution I dont see the advantage of moving it.  Pop riviting is an excellent idea. I was thinking of bolting it somehow but I like your idea better.||||reg||1
